    ['I','01','What is a planned neighborhood?','A planned neighborhood is the synthesis of a project that puts people at the centre of everything.',
      ['At Parc Autódromo, every detail is designed to integrate living, leisure, work, education and security in a single place, so life flows and your time and well-being come first on every corner.','Its real differentiator is proximity: the school, the market, the park, all just minutes away. Wide streets, bike paths and connected leisure areas let you walk, cycle and move with ease, in a place where cars no longer dominate and people are in control of the space.'],'escola.html',''],
    ['I','02','The urbanism of Jaime Lerner','&ldquo;The greatest attraction of a city is the quality of life of its people.&rdquo;',
      ['Few names in urbanism carry the weight of Jaime Lerner. Architect, urbanist and three-time mayor of Curitiba, he devoted his life to reinventing how cities work for people. Parc Autódromo is one more proof of that vision, urbanism designed to raise quality of life, with well-being and human coexistence as the priority.','Density, diversity, identity. Mobility, coexistence, sustainability. Wide streets, tree-lined parks and shared spaces reflect what Lerner always saw in cities, places that foster exchange and collective well-being. Parc is the continuation of that legacy, and one of his final projects.'],'aerial.html','<div class="sc-arch"><img loading="lazy" src="'+B+'lerner.jpg?v=2" alt="Jaime Lerner"><div class="sc-arch-meta"><b>Jaime Lerner</b><span>Architect &amp; urbanist · Curitiba, 1937–2021</span></div></div>'],
